<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Photisarath</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1501–1547</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Photisarath I, Phothisarath</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Photisarath was king of Lan Xang from 1520 to 1547, a devout Buddhist who in 1527 ordered the suppression of spirit cults in favour of Buddhist practice. He married a princess of Lan Na, which allowed his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/setthathirath">Setthathirath</a> to claim the Lan Na throne, and he died in an accident while capturing an elephant.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/photisarath.jpg" alt="Photisarath" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kittipong khunnen · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Phra_That_Phanom_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
